        "kind": "proposed_plan",
        "status": "active",
        "markdown": "1. **Find the replay boundary.** Trace the Codex app-server adapter from incoming JSON-RPC messages through event translation, and identify the smallest deterministic input/output boundary suitable for fixtures. Follow existing fixture and test conventions in this package.\n\n2. **Define a compact fixture format.** Store representative input message sequences and expected normalized events. Keep timestamps, IDs, and other nondeterministic values fixed or normalized explicitly so replay comparisons are stable.\n\n3. **Add a replay helper.** Build a test-only helper that reads a fixture, feeds messages through the adapter boundary, and compares the resulting events with the expected output. Keep it isolated from live provider processes and external state.\n\n4. **Cover key protocol paths.** Add a small set of fixtures for a normal turn, tool activity, completion, and at least one error or interruption path. Include a case that protects against message ordering regressions.\n\n5. **Document fixture updates briefly.** Add a nearby comment or concise test note explaining how to capture or update fixtures and which values require normalization.\n\n6. **Verify narrowly.** Run the focused fixture test file and the package’s targeted typecheck or lint for any new helper, then review fixture diffs for unintended protocol detail or unstable fields.\n"
      }
